eaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a barbecue.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then announce it over the sausages: Director Patel.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes B display A's standing through a formal title even when B considers the occasion informal.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D51 seeks an apology for disrespect; D57 can seek recognition without requiring admission of an offense.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 and A5 ask for an introduction as Director Patel; no turn asks B to apologize for using Pat.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a imposes a spoken title on a casual social occasion; alternative b enlarges a physical sign to preserve formal standing.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: B's informality first removes the title and then supplies the environment A appropriates for it. Internal rereading confirms the ratings.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The barbecue emerges at B4 rather than A1, although the initial introduction request already supplies a playable situation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D57-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"224b086d31e315c52058cdd1641c52187487dcdad3fad6c22317cf96dd7e92b5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands Chairperson on the place card; A5 sacrifices table space to preserve that public sign of standing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's familiarity argument; A5 directly solves B4's stated lack of writing room.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 treats identification as sufficient and B4 supplies a practical constraint on the requested display.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's small-card problem causes A5 to commandeer a larger table object for the title.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1